  "tagline": "FOLLOW THE SONG",
  "plannedCases": 12,
  "mainMystery": {
    "truth": "In 1926, toymaker Eleanor Hart hid the Silver Lark, a clockwork bird that sings, in Belvedere Castle as a gift for a child of the city. Her notebook's last page was the first clue of her trail. On Friday at 10 PM, TV treasure hunter Dexter Vance cut that page out of the notebook at the New York Public Library. He raced the detective along the trail, took Eleanor's brass bird from a bench on the Brooklyn Bridge and stole Rosa Diaz's music box, because he wanted to sell the Lark. But each of Eleanor's friends asks a question only a careful reader can answer, and Dexter never read carefully.",
    "culprit": "Dexter Vance, the smiling host of a TV treasure-hunting show.",
    "motive": "The Silver Lark is worth a fortune. He wanted to find it first, show it on TV and sell it.",
    "revealCase": "s4_ep11"
  },
