  "notes": [
    "Season 4, planned by Claude Code with tool/season_planner (PLAYBOOK.md) and carried into the game by the create-season skill from the input 'Season 4, New York'.",
    "The Hart Building (Bleecker Street, Greenwich Village) and its clock shop are made up for the story; every other place is a real place in New York. The Golden Lantern Tea House and the TV studio are made up, in real neighbourhoods.",
    "Real facts the puzzles lean on: Grand Central's ceiling shows the stars back to front, its information booth has a four-faced clock and the station has a Lost and Found; the Wonder Wheel at Coney Island (1920) has cars that swing and cars that stay still; Belvedere Castle stands on a rock above a pond in Central Park.",
    "art.map (assets/seasons/season_04_newyork/locations/map/newyork_map.png) is written once the map is made, its landmarks measured on it (season_factory step 6), never guessed."
  ]
